#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the documentation for the &kde; &systemsettings; module that configures graphic tablets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"

#. Tag: keyword
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "System Settings"
msgstr "Systeeminstellen"

#. Tag: keyword
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wacom"
msgstr "Wacom"

#. Tag: keyword
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tablet"
msgstr "Tablett"

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wacom Tablet Settings"
msgstr "Wacom-Tablett instellen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tablet &systemsettings; module handles all setting for your graphic tablet. All tablets supported by the <ulink url=\"http://linuxwacom.sourceforge.net\">&Linux; Wacom driver</ulink> project are handled by this settings interface. Make sure your tablet is detected either via xorg.conf or HAL and works in general. Refer to the <link linkend=\"detection\">tablet detection</link> section for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <application>wacom-tools</application> or the <application>xf86-input-wacom</application> driver must be installed on your computer and <command>xsetwacom</command> must be available in order to make this module work correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "The module is split into various tab pages that handle all aspects of your tablet and the pen: <link linkend=\"tablet-profiles\">Profiles</link>, <link linkend=\"tablet-general\">General Information</link>, <link linkend=\"pad-buttons\">Pad Buttons</link>, <link linkend=\"pad-mapping\">Pad Mapping</link>, <link linkend=\"screen-setup\">Screen Setup</link>, <link linkend=\"stylus\">Stylus Settings</link> and <link linkend=\"eraser\">Eraser Settings</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Profile Management"
msgstr "Profilpleeg"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the small drop down box with the two buttons next to it. You can create new profiles and delete already existing ones. Each profile is saved and specified for the currently connected tablet. If you create a new profile, it automatically creates one with the default settings as returned by the wacom-tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can specify different profiles for your settings. For example if you like to have a different behavior of the pen when you use it as a mouse replacement for your day to day work or using it as pen to draw something."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each profile can be changed on the fly and directly changes the behavior of your tablet input."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <link linkend=\"kded\">kded tablet daemon</link> must be running in the background to be able to change the profiles and apply them to the tablet. All the work is done by the daemon. The &systemsettings; module just change the profile settings for it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Tablet Settings and Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows some general Information about the detected tablet. Beside the name and company of your tablet an image is shown and all detected input devices are listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tablet must be connected and the <link linkend=\"kded\">kded</link> must be running to allow the module to work correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "See the <link linkend=\"troubles\">Detection problems</link> section for further help on the tablet detection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pad Button Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can set different actions for each pad button, the touch ring or touch strip on your tablet if available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:119 index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available actions are:"
msgstr "Disse Akschonen sünd verföögbor:"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:123 index.docbook:260
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Disable</guilabel> : disables the button."
msgstr "<guilabel>Utmaken</guilabel>: Maakt de Tast ut"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:129 index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Button</guilabel> : emulates a general button event press."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:135 index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Keystroke</guilabel> : emulates a keystroke or special key press (for example <keycap>F1</keycap> or <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:141 index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>QuoteDbl</guilabel> : emulates a text string. For example you could print <quote>Hello World</quote> at the current cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pad Mapping Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "This pages change the behavior of the tablet working area. It can be rotated and reduced in size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Working area</guilabel> spans the whole tablet by default. The <guilabel>Top X/Y</guilabel> and <guilabel>Bottom X/Y</guilabel> coordinates can be changed to change the aspect ratio of the tablet and thus match the screen ratio."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will setup your tablet to match your screens. The multi monitor setup is realized via Nvidia TwinView support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>TwinView</guilabel> : Nvidia TwinView option. Select how to connect your multi monitor setup. You need to specify the right screen resolutions as well, otherwise it won't work as you expect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Resolution</guilabel> : Specifies the Meta Mode for the monitors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Multi Monitor</guilabel> : Turns on/off across monitor movement in multi-monitor desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Map to screen</guilabel> : Maps the cursor to a specific monitor if across monitor movement is switched off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "The button actions screen toggle and display toggle change the multi monitor behavior on the fly. See the <link linkend=\"stylus\">stylus</link> section for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stylus Settings"
msgstr "Stift instellen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "The pen that is used together with the tablet has two different sides, the main side is called stylus. With this dialog you can change any aspect of the stylus side and the buttons on the pen to adjust them to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cursor Settings"
msgstr "Wieser instellen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Mode</guilabel> : Change the pen mode between absolute and relative input. Relative acts more like a mouse while absolute is like a pen on the paper position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Speed</guilabel> : Sets relative cursor movement speed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Threshold</guilabel> : Sets tip/eraser pressure threshold."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Pressure</guilabel> : Change the press curve. The curve is shown in a new dialog and you can change the Bézier curve with the red dots. The curve defines how the pressure of the pen is translated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use your pen inside the press curve dialog to see the changes in the press curve directly. A blue area below the curve shows the applied pressure of the pen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tip Double Click Distance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defines how fast you need to tap the tip of the pen on the tablet to be recognize it as a double click instead of two single clicks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "Button Settings"
msgstr "Knoopinstellen"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lets you map the tip and the two additional buttons on your pen with different actions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Left Click</guilabel> : emulates a left mouse button click event."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Middle Click</guilabel> : emulates a middle mouse button click event."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Right Click</guilabel> : emulates a right mouse button click event."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Double Click</guilabel> : emulates a double click event."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Mode Toggle</guilabel> : change the pen mode between absolute and relative input. Relative acts more like a mouse while absolute is like a pen on the paper position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Screen Toggle</guilabel> : If more than one screen is connected and TwinView is deactivated this allows you to switch the current used screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Display Toggle</guilabel> : Toggles between multi monitor and single monitor mode. Thus allows to move from one screen to another."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Eraser Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you turn around the pen it will be recognized as eraser instead as pen. This allows to change the settings independent to the stylus side. All parameters are as described in the <link linkend=\"stylus\">stylus</link> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tablet daemon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tablet daemon runs in the background and does the ground work. Detecting the tablet and set it up with the selected profiles. If the daemon is not running the &systemsettings; module and the plasma applet cannot work properly and the tablet cannot be used with the profiles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tablet detection"
msgstr "Tablett-Opdecken"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "The detection of the <hardware>tablet device</hardware> is done in several ways. <application>Solid</application> is used in the first step and does the hotplug support. If Solid fails the next steps are <command>xsetwacom list dev</command>, <command>lsusb</command> and <command>xinput --list</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Should none of the commands above return the name of the tablet, it is not supported and cannot be used by this module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detection problems"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "If the tablet is not detected check the <ulink url=\"http://linuxwacom.sourceforge.net\">&Linux; Wacom driver</ulink> page if your tablet is supported. Furthermore check via <command>lsusb</command> if you can find your tablet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "If HAL does not handle the detection add the tablet to your <filename>/etc/X11/xorg.conf</filename> file and restart the x-server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid "In case of a serial device (Tablet PC and such) check if <command>xinput --list</command> lists your input devices (Stylus/Eraser/Pad). Should they be listed take a look at the internal tablet device id via <command>xsetwacom get \"Name of your pad or stylus\" TabletID</command>. If an id is returned please mail all the necessary information to the author."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hotplug support is only available if the tablet is found via <application>Solid</application> and its notification API."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "<application>Solid</application> checks if the value for the entry <command>input.x11_options.Type</command> is <command>pen</command>, <command>stylus</command>, <command>eraser</command> or <command>cursor</command> or if the value for the entry <command>input.x11_driver</command> is <command>wacom</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Please mail the author if your tablet is detected by Solid but with other values to enhance the tablet support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tablet plasma applet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tablet applet makes it possible to change the available profiles on the fly. Furthermore you can change the pad rotation and switch between absolute/relative mode of the stylus/eraser regardless of the current profile settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is not necessary to add the plasmoid for this module to work. The default profile will be activated by the <link linkend=\"kded\">tablet daemon</link> as soon as it detects your tablet even if the plasmoid is not used. The plasmoid is just a visual helper to switch easily between the profiles."
msgstr ""

